{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To determine which of the given vectors are possible direction vectors for a line with slope \\(-\\frac{7}{4}\\), we need to recall that the slope of a line can also be represented by the ratio of the y-component to the x-component of its direction vector. Specifically, if a vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}\\) is a direction vector for the line, then the slope \\(m\\) of the line is given by \\(\\frac{b}{a}\\).\n\nGiven that the slope of the line is \\(-\\frac{7}{4}\\), we need to find vectors \\(\\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}\\) such that \\(\\frac{b}{a} = -\\frac{7}{4}\\). This implies that \\(b = -\\frac{7}{4}a\\). We will check each option to see if it satisfies this condition.\n\n(A) \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n\\[\n\\frac{7}{4} \\neq -\\frac{7}{4}\n\\]\nThis vector is not a direction vector.\n\n(B) \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\)\n\\[\n\\frac{4}{7} \\neq -\\frac{7}{4}\n\\]\nThis vector is not a direction vector.\n\n","prefix_end":930,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,8253,892,315,279,2661,22879,525,3204,5106,22879,369,264,1555,448,30232,1124,4080,59,37018,90,22,15170,19,11035,701,582,1184,311,19091,429,279,30232,315,264,1555,646,1083,387,15251,553,279,11341,315,279,379,41387,311,279,856,41387,315,1181,5106,4621,13,44763,11,421,264,4621,1124,11520,7265,90,5187,2555,92,264,24984,293,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,8,374,264,5106,4621,369,279,1555,11,1221,279,30232,17767,76,57758,315,279,1555,374,2661,553,1124,11520,37018,90,65,15170,64,11035,3593,22043,429,279,30232,315,279,1555,374,1124,4080,59,37018,90,22,15170,19,11035,701,582,1184,311,1477,22879,1124,11520,7265,90,5187,2555,92,264,24984,293,1124,408,90,5187,2555,11035,8,1741,429,1124,11520,37018,90,65,15170,64,92,284,481,59,37018,90,22,15170,19,11035,568,1096,23945,429,17767,65,284,481,59,37